      "text": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n𝑥\n\t\n=\n−\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n−\n2\n)\n−\n2\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n2\n−\n4\n)\n+\n1\n\n\n𝑦\n\t\n=\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n+\n2\n)\n+\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n2\n−\n4\n)\n−\n1\n\n\t\n−\n2\n≤\n𝑡\n≤\n2\n\nChoose an answer\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n✓\nCorrect choice selected.\nCORRECT\nPreview only\nSolution:\n\nAnswer · correct value:\n\nFirst calculate the \n𝑥\n-values using \n𝑥\n=\n−\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n−\n2\n)\n−\n2\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n2\n−\n4\n)\n+\n1\n:\n\n𝑡\n\t\n−\n2\n\t\n−\n1\n\t\n0\n\t\n1\n\t\n2\n\n\n𝑥\n\t\n−\n7\n\t\n−\n8\n\t\n1\n\t\n8\n\t\n1\n\n\n𝑦\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\nNow calculate \n𝑦\n=\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n+\n2\n)\n+\n𝑡\n(\n𝑡\n2\n−\n4\n)\n−\n1\n at the same parameter values:\n\n𝑡\n\t\n−\n2\n\t\n−\n1\n\t\n0\n\t\n1\n\t\n2\n\n\n𝑥\n\t\n−\n7\n\t\n−\n8\n\t\n1\n\t\n8\n\t\n1\n\n\n𝑦\n\t\n−\n1\n\t\n1\n\t\n−\n1\n\t\n−\n1\n\t\n7\n\nThe successive paired points are \n(\n−\n7\n,\n−\n1\n)\n, \n(\n−\n8\n,\n1\n)\n, \n(\n1\n,\n−\n1\n)\n, \n(\n8\n,\n−\n1\n)\n, \n(\n1\n,\n7\n)\n. Use the endpoint pair to find the matching group, then compare an interior paired point to distinguish the remaining curves.\n\nBack to study →",
